  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 204 AM CDT Wed Sep 30 2026\n\nUpper-level ridging will build across the desert southwest through \nthe upcoming weekend into early next week. A dry northwest flow \naloft will become established atop our area on the northeast \nperiphery of the high. At the surface, Canadian high pressure will \nbe located across the central and northern plains Friday. This will \nusher in a cooler, drier Canadian airmass. Temperatures Friday will \naverage below normal with highs in the 60s. As the high shifts east \nof the area Saturday, gusty south winds develop ahead of a weak \napproaching shortwave and associated surface low across western \nSouth Dakota. As the surface low shifts east across South Dakota \nSaturday afternoon and evening, a cold front will switch winds to \nthe north. Saturday's highs will moderate into the upper 60s to mid \n70s, but then cool back into the 60s Sunday behind the front. No \nprecipitation is expected with the weak shortwave and cold front, as \nthe atmosphere will be quite dry. \n\nEarly next week, gusty south winds return Monday into Tuesday. \nTemperatures will moderate back to near or even slightly above \nnormal By Tuesday, when highs could top 80 degrees across western \ninto southwest Nebraska.",
